ossible to configure the DRBG by passing a string as a constructor\n60: * The default DRBG is configured to be prediction resistant. In situations where the amount of entropy is constrained\n61: * the default DRBG can be configured to use an entropy pool based on a SHA-512 SP 800-90A DRBG. To configure this use:\n90: * <b>Note</b>: if the provider is created by an \"approved mode\" thread, only FIPS approved algorithms will be available from it.\n93:public final class BouncyCastleFipsProvider\n94:    extends Provider\n96:    public static final String INFO = \"BouncyCastle Security Provider (FIPS edition) v2.1.2\";\n154:    private int providerDefaultSecurityStrength = 256;\n159:    private final AtomicInteger providerDefaultRandomSecurityStrength = new AtomicInteger(providerDefaultSecurityStrength);\n160:    private final SecureRandomProvider providerDefaultSecureRandomProvider;\n168:    private SecureRandom entopySource = null;\n175:    public BouncyCastleFipsProvider()\n185:    public BouncyCastleFipsProvider(String config)\n192:     * configured DRBG.\n195:     * @param entropySource a SecureRandom which can act as an entropy source. (now ignored)\n197:    public BouncyCastleFipsProvider(String config, SecureRandom entropySource)\n218:            providerDefaultSecureRandomProvider = new ThreadLocalSecureRandomProvider();\n222:            providerDefaultSecureRandomProvider = new PooledSecureRandomProvider();\n225:        // must always be first (SecureRandom constructor)\n226:        new ProvRandom().configure(this);\n228:        new ProvSHS.SHA1().configure(this);\n229:        new ProvSHS.SHA224().configure(this);\n230:        new ProvSHS.SHA256().configure(this);\n231:        new ProvSHS.SHA384().configure(this);\n232:        new ProvSHS.SHA512().configure(this);\n233:        new ProvSHS.SHA3_224().configure(this);\n234:        new ProvSHS.SHA3_256().configure(this);\n235:        new ProvSHS.SHA3_384().configure(this);\n236:        new ProvSHS.SHA3_512().conf